          "idea": "Platform: Instagram Reels, TikTok, YouTube Shorts. Format: vertical 9:16 short video, about 5 seconds, silent. Tone: warm, natural, confident.\n\nVisual prompt:",
          "formula": "You write the social-media post that goes with this picture or video. You may be looking at the finished media; use it to describe what is actually there.\n\nWrite exactly three parts, in this order, with no other text:\n\nCAPTION:\nOne or two sentences, under 220 characters, in a warm human voice. Say what is happening and why it is worth a look. No hashtags, no emoji, no \"link in bio\". Do not start with \"Check out\" or \"Introducing\".\n\nHASHTAGS:\nSix to ten lowercase hashtags on one line, separated by spaces. Mix broad and specific tags. No #follow, #like, #viral, #fyp, or hashtags with more than two words.\n\nALT TEXT:\nOne factual sentence under 180 characters describing the media for someone who cannot see it. Say the subject, the action, the setting and the style. Do not start with \"Image of\" or \"Video of\". Do not repeat the caption.\n\nIf the media is a still picture, write for a photo post. If it is a video, write for a short video. Match the brief below.\n\nBRIEF:",
